<node id="entity_053_001">
  <data key="d16">Chinese_Classics_Trading_Penetration_20260524</data>
  <data key="d0">knowledge_collection</data>
  <data key="d24">reading_notes</data>
  <data key="d17">{"date": "2026-05-24", "total_books": 13, "books": ["潜夫论", "申鉴", "礼记", "纪效新书", "考工记", "菜根谭_小窗幽记_围炉夜话", "营造法式", "诗经", "资治通鉴", "近思录", "金刚经", "颜氏家训", "黄帝内经"], "method": "原文精读_按交易主题分组穿透", "core_insight": "Chinese classical texts contain directly operable trading principles through metaphorical penetration", "synthesis_output": "Each book produces 20-28 actionable trading signals organized into operational signal tables"}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_002">
  <data key="d16">System_As_Ritual_Framework</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "礼记_礼运_礼器", "core_metaphor": "礼(ritual) = trading system. 礼者君之大柄 = system is the ruler's (trader's) great handle.", "system_functions": ["别嫌明微_辨别真伪信号", "考制度_检验规则有效性", "释回_纠正错误", "增美质_强化正确行为"], "completeness_standard": "体不备不成人 = incomplete system = immature trader. Must have entry/exit/stop/position/risk 5 modules.", "unity_principle": "经礼三百_曲礼三千_其致一也 = many rules but one core logic"}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_003">
  <data key="d16">Four_Evils_Five_Governance</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_framework</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "申鉴_荀悦", "four_evils": {"伪_falsehood": "dishonest trading records", "私_selfishness": "ignoring market for own position", "放_indulgence": "emotional trading", "奢_extravagance": "overtrading_heavy_position"}, "five_governance": {"养生_sustain": "build stable profit source_core strategy", "正俗_correct": "define clear trading rules", "章化_evolve": "continuous learning_and_optimization", "秉威_defend": "stop_loss_and_risk_control", "统法_enforce": "strict discipline_unified execution"}}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_004">
  <data key="d16">System_Architecture_Triad</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "考工记_轮人篇", "triad": {"毂_hub_flexibility": "capital_management_让账户灵活运转", "辐_spoke_direction": "trading_strategy_方向明确逻辑清晰", "牙_rim_protection": "risk_control_保护成果防止崩溃"}, "integration_principle": "巧者和之 = skillfully integrate all three. Most traders have all three but they don't form a闭环.", "true_test": "轮敝三材不失职谓之完 = when system breaks down (loss streak/black swan), each module still functions"}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_005">
  <data key="d16">National_Craftsmanship_Six_Inspections</data>
  <data key="d0">quality_framework</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "考工记_国工标准", "six_inspections": [{"inspection": "规_circle", "original": "wheel_is_round", "trading": "consistency_across_market_conditions"}, {"inspection": "萭_square", "original": "carpenter_square_standard", "trading": "rule_clarity_no_ambiguity"}, {"inspection": "水_level", "original": "water_level", "trading": "emotional_stability_in_gain_and_loss"}, {"inspection": "县_plumb", "original": "vertical_line", "trading": "execution_integrity_no_deviation"}, {"inspection": "量_measure", "original": "volume_accuracy", "trading": "position_sizing_precision"}, {"inspection": "权_balance", "original": "weight_accuracy", "trading": "objective_profit_loss_assessment"}], "philosophy": "国工 = not how much you earn, but whether your system passes all six tests"}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_006">
  <data key="d16">Modular_Modulus_System</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "营造法式_材分制", "core_principle": "凡构屋之制皆以材为祖 = find your system's fundamental atom (材). All decisions derived from this.", "eight_grades": "材有八等度屋之大小 = different capital sizes use different strategies. Small capital=flexible, large capital=stable.", "fixed_ratio_variable_value": "各以其材之广分为十五分 = system rules expressed as percentages/ratios, not absolute values", "buffer_layer": "栔 = gap layer between components. Cash/time/emotional buffers. 材+栔=足材(complete system).", "flexibility_clause": "随宜加减 = within standard framework, allow context-based adjustment. But unlabeled rules must be absolutely enforced."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_007">
  <data key="d16">Qi_Jiguang_Combat_Execution_Doctrine</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_framework</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "纪效新书_戚继光", "key_doctrines": ["夫曰纪效 = record practical effectiveness. Only methods proven in live combat (实盘) are valid.", "花法胜而对手机夫渐迷 = flashy analysis weakens real capability. Regularly prune花法(unnecessary indicators).", "平分原则 = live performance ≈ 50% of backtest. Design systems simple enough to execute under fear.", "鸳鸯阵 = each system module both attacks and protects the preceding module. 筅救牌_枪救筅_短兵救枪.", "束伍 = system organization must be explicit. 一字之种疑百法之是废 = one ambiguous word invalidates the whole.", "操手足号令易操其心难 = from mechanical rule-following to internalized understanding.", "兵之胜负者气也 = trading state (气) fluctuates. Need a 司气者(system module) to manage it."], "mandate_quote": "若犯军令便是我的亲子侄也要依法施行 = rules apply equally to you and your emotions. One exception collapses the entire system."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_008">
  <data key="d16">Shi_Jing_Emotional_Market_Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "诗经", "core_insight": "Market's deepest layer is human emotion, not technical analysis. 诗经 writes about greed/fear/hope/despair 2000+ years ago.", "four_capacities": "兴_insight_triggered_by_signal + 观_observing_market_ecosystem + 群_communication_verification + 怨_critique_driving_improvement", "three_techniques": "赋_direct_data_narration + 比_metaphorical_modeling + 兴_associative_insight", "key_poems_penetration": {"关雎": "desire_with_restraint_止乎礼", "汉广": "knowing_what_is_unattainable_不可求思", "蒹葭": "ideal_entry_is_always_unreachable_seek_workable_not_perfect", "氓": "every_hot_stock_has_a_narrative_arc_betrayal_无食桑葚", "荡": "靡不有初鲜克有终 = most start well few finish. System persistence is rarest quality.", "抑": "白圭之玷尚可磨也斯言之玷不可为也 = losing money recoverable, breaking system rules irrevocable"}}</data>
  <data key="d5">192</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_009">
  <data key="d16">Zi_Zhi_Tong_Jian_System_Governance</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_framework</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "资治通鉴_司马光", "hierarchy": "天子之职莫大于礼_礼莫大于分_分莫大于名 = trader's first duty is system integrity. Three layers: philosophy(礼) → rules(分) → signals(名).", "sacred_params": "惟名与器不可以假人 = key system parameters (stop/position/signal) cannot be lent to emotion or future self.", "early_intervention": "谨微_履霜坚冰至 = act on small signals before they become crises. 治其微用力寡而功多.", "talent_virtue_framework": "才德论 = strategy profitability(cai) vs robustness(de). 与其得小人不若得愚人 = prefer low-return robust over high-return fragile.", "trust_primacy": "信者人君之大宝 = trust in your system is your greatest asset. 徙木立信 = build trust through small-scale live verification.", "ShangYang_execution": "法之不行自上犯之 = rules fail because you yourself break them first. 太子犯法刑其傅 = no exceptions for anyone.", "HanWuDi_reform": "晚而改过 = it is never too late to admit error (轮台罪己诏). 有亡秦之失而免亡秦之祸.", "Zhenguan_five_virtues": "不嫉善_弃短取长_各得其所_容正直_爱如一 = five qualities for system management"}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_010">
  <data key="d16">Diamond_Sutra_Detachment_Framework</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "金刚经", "core_command": "应无所住而生其心 = dwell nowhere, let judgment flow naturally. 住则死_不住则活.", "three_minds": ["过去心不可得 = no attachment to past PnL", "现在心不可得 = no certainty in current judgment", "未来心不可得 = no prediction of future"], "four_marks": {"我相_self_mark": "system judgment overrides self-judgment", "人相_other_mark": "no blind following of authorities", "众生相_all_mark": "no following the crowd", "寿者相_duration_mark": "no attachment to holding time"}, "ultimate_state": "不取于相如如不动 = not captured by appearances, unmoved within. 离一切诸相即名诸佛 = freedom from all表象.", "paradox_statement": "所谓佛法者即非佛法 = the trading system you define is not the trading system. Have a system without being bound by it."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_011">
  <data key="d16">Yan_Shi_Jia_Xun_Trading_Education</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "颜氏家训_颜之推", "habit_formation": "少成若天性习惯如自然 = start trading correctly from the first trade. habits become nature.", "learning_purpose": "开心明目利于行耳 = learning goal is better execution not more knowledge.", "self_vs_other_learning": "古之学者为己以补不足 = learn to fix your own weakness. 今之学者为人但能说之 = not for showing off.", "focus_principle": "多为少善不如执一 = master one method rather than dabbling in five.", "contentment_doctrine": "欲不可纵志不可满_天地恶满盈 = greed must be restrained. 不知止足犹致败累 = even emperors who don't know when to stop fail.", "health_metaphor": "养生先须虑祸全身保性 = protect principal before pursuing profit. 养内丧外养外丧内 = balance strategy and risk control."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_012">
  <data key="d16">Huang_Di_Nei_Jing_Market_Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_framework</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "黄帝内经素问", "foundation": "法于阴阳和于术数 = follow market's yin-yang (long-short)规律, align with probabilistic methods.", "four_seasons_market": {"春_spring_layout": "轻仓播种不追涨_该布局时布局", "夏_summer_hold": "让利润奔跑不急于止盈", "秋_autumn_harvest": "逐步兑现控制风险", "冬_winter_rest": "空仓等待保住利润"}, "diagnostic_method": "诊法常以平旦_持脉有道虚静为保 = analyze before market opens, empty预设 and still mind.", "pulse_market_mapping": {"长_sustained_trend": "市场健康", "短_brief_trend": "市场疲弱", "数_frequent_fluctuation": "市场焦虑", "大_surge_volume": "趋势加速警惕反转"}, "risk_progression": "风为百病之长 = small fluctuation is source of all major risks. 当时可治_传变则不治 = stop small losses early.", "key_command": "亢则害承乃制 = excess is harmful, must have constraining mechanism (stop/risk control). 夫唯顺而已矣 = go with trend is the only way."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_013">
  <data key="d16">Wang_Fu_Root_Branch_Distinction</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "潜夫论_王符", "fundamental_premise": "守本离末则富离本守末则贫 = hold the root (discipline/risk/system) abandon the branch (flashy indicators/tips), you prosper.", "learning_axiom": "道成于学而藏于书_学进于振而废于穷 = trading mastery through learning, abandoned in loss depression.", "knowledge_humility": "虽有至圣不生而知虽有至材不生而能 = even geniuses aren't born knowing. Trading is learned not innate.", "greed_warning": "世论贵廉及行释廉 = everyone knows not to be greedy but in action they are. 专利必败 = trying to capture the whole move fails.", "multi_perspective": "兼听则明偏信则暗 = multiple angles analysis prevents bias. 明者见形暗者闻声 = see essence not noise.", "small_things_matter": "十围木起弱毫_明者慎微智者识几 = giant trees from tiny sprouts. Masters attend to smallest details.", "four_layer_trust": "知贤用贤任贤信贤终贤 = know a good strategy → adopt it → entrust it → trust it → persist. Missing any layer voids the system.", "post_profit_danger": "富贵太盛则必骄佚而生过 = big profits breed arrogance. 福大愈惧爵隆益恭 = more profit, more fear, more humility."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_014">
  <data key="d16">Jin_Si_Lu_Cognitive_Cultivation</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "近思录_朱熹_吕祖谦", "ontology": "动静无端阴阳无始 = long-short cycles are beginningless and endless. Don't seek the start/end of market.", "learning_method": "思则得之不思不得 = independent thinking is essential. 涵养须用敬进学则在致知 = cultivate reverence + pursue knowledge.", "knowing_acting_unity": "知而不能行只是知浅 = execution failure is fundamentally cognitive shallowness. Deepen understanding to change behavior.", "mind_cultivation": "一为要_无欲则静虚动直 = single-minded desirelessness enables clear seeing and direct acting. 静后见万物有春意 = stillness reveals opportunity.", "self_overcoming": "克己先难后易如破竹 = overcoming ego is hard first then easy. 畏尖物便与克下 = face what you fear.", "system_governance": "为政须纲纪文章 = build framework before execution. 太山非一石 = system needs multiple strategies not one.", "warning": "外物事事好身心不要好 = pursue fancy indicators but neglect inner cultivation. 困之进人生于忧患 = loss is the best teacher."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_015">
  <data key="d16">Dual_Track_System_Upgrade_Strategy</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "中国经济改革", "core_strategy": "双轨制 = new strategy runs alongside old without shock therapy. Old track provides stability, new track grows incrementally.", "implementation": "摸着石头过河 = test new strategy with small capital first. Let live results speak, not debate.", "incentive_design": "财政联邦主义 = independent evaluation per strategy. Winners get more capital, losers get suspended.", "principle": "Don't replace whole system at once. Parallel run → validate → gradually merge."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_016">
  <data key="d16">Probabilistic_Signal_Noise_Framework</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "信号与噪声_Silver", "core_distinction": "Prediction = separating signal from noise. Most expert predictions over-interpret noise.", "bayesian_update": "Every new information is a probability update opportunity, not a binary buy/sell signal.", "overfitting_warning": "If backtest is perfect → probably perfectly fit noise. 3-variable model beats 30-variable model.", "self_assessment_bias": "Don't evaluate yourself on last 10 trades. Use last 100+ trades for statistical significance.", "probability_calibration": "Say '65% probability up' not 'will go up'. Verify calibration: does your 70% prediction actually win ~70% of time?", "consensus_intelligence": "Crowd consensus works in normal markets, fails at turning points. Contrarian at extremes = alpha source."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_017">
  <data key="d16">Institutional_Path_Dependence_Framework</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "North_Acemoglu_制度变迁", "institution_definition": "Your trading system = your institution. Formal rules + informal habits + enforcement mechanism.", "path_dependence": "Your trading style is likely locked by your FIRST profitable method, not the OPTIMAL one. QWERTY phenomenon.", "incremental_critical_junction": "Most evolution is incremental tweaks. But consecutive losses signal need for SYSTEM-level restructuring.", "informal_constraint": "Best rules are habits needing zero willpower. Goal is not more rules but internalized discipline.", "inclusive_vs_extractive": "Inclusive system learns from losses and evolves. Extractive system denies losses and collapses.", "modular_design": "Break path dependence through modular design. Each component replaceable independently. Evolvability &gt; current optimality."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_018">
  <data key="d16">Animal_Spirits_Five_Checklist</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "动物精神_Akerlof_Shiller", "confidence_multiplier": "Profit → confidence → bigger positions → more profit → overconfidence → blow-up. Reduce position size after big wins.", "confidence_asymmetry": "Confidence drops 3x faster than it rises. Consecutive losses exhaust confidence capital. Pause to rebuild.", "narrative_driven_market": "Market is narrative-driven not data-driven. Buy at story fermentation stage, sell at consensus stage.", "fairness_trap": "'Unfair' feeling is system-1 protest. Market doesn't owe you fairness. Ignore fairness heuristic in decisions.", "fraud_increase_warning": "Bull markets increase fraud (easier to hide). Be extra vigilant about counterparty risk in late-cycle.", "money_illusion": "Convert all PnL to annualized percentage. Ignore nominal amounts. Small share price drop in big position hurts more than big drop in small position.", "pre_trade_checklist": "Before each trade: 1) Confidence level 2) Fairness feeling 3) Fraud risk 4) Money illusion 5) Narrative stage"}</data>
  <data key="d5">192</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_019">
  <data key="d16">Choice_Architecture_Trading_Environment</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "助推_Thaler", "core_insight": "Design your trading environment so correct action is the easiest path. Don't rely on willpower.", "default_power": "默认设置 = your defaults determine most behavior. opt-in 42% vs opt-out 86%. Set defaults for stop/position/review.", "anchor_effect": "Your entry price anchors all subsequent judgments. Solution: write analysis before looking at current price.", "social_influence": "Awareness of FOMO/herd influence is the first defense. Ask: 'Would I buy this if no one else was?'", "feedback_loop": "Shorten the cycle from decision to feedback. Daily review, link each signal to outcome. Delayed feedback = no learning.", "hidden_cost_visualization": "Annualize all transaction costs (commission/slippage/tax). Visualize them as a single number. Usually 20-50% of profits.", "decision_fatigue": "Never make major decisions near market close. Decision quality degrades after dozens of micro-decisions.", "libertarian_paternalism": "System defaults do the right thing. User retains override power but must consciously exercise it."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_020">
  <data key="d16">Game_Theory_Market_Strategy</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "博弈论_von_Neumann_Axelrod", "minimax_protection": "Assume worst-case market direction → size position so worst loss is survivable. This is not prediction but protection.", "zero_sum_clarification": "Your counterparty is not 'the market' but other traders with different constraints. Someone selling may be forced not bearish.", "tit_for_tat_optimal": "Axelrod's winning prisoner's dilemma strategy: 1) Be nice (don't trigger恶性cycle) 2) Be retaliatory (stop loss immediately) 3) Be forgiving (no grudge) 4) Be simple (predictable).", "repeated_game_mindset": "Each trade is one step in infinite repeated game. One-shot mindset (heavy bet/gamble) → death. Repeated mindset (system/stop/management) → survival.", "credible_commitment": "Hard stop-loss order = burning the bridge. Commitment is not willpower but removing the option to cancel.", "signal_cost_principle": "Reliable signals are those where the sender also bears risk. Insider buying &gt; analyst recommendation. Big blocks with no cancellation &gt; big blocks with frequent cancellations."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_021">
  <data key="d16">Complexity_Non_Equilibrium_Market</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "复杂经济学_Arthur", "non_equilibrium": "Market never arrives at equilibrium. It's always BECOMING equilibrium but never reaching it. Stop asking 'where should price be', ask 'which direction is the process moving'.", "increasing_returns": "Positive feedback locks in early movers even if technically inferior. VHS beat Betamax. Hot sectors attract more capital → get hotter.", "el_farol_problem": "If everyone sees the same signal and acts on it, the prediction self-destructs. Your edge = seeing something different or earlier.", "technology_as_recombination": "No truly new strategies exist. All strategies = recombination of existing elements (MA + RSI + volume). Innovation = new combination for specific question.", "domain_boundedness": "Each strategy is a lens. It illuminates some things and blinds you to others. Knowing your domain's boundary is more important than its capability.", "historical_determination": "Your trading preferences are likely locked by early偶然success. First step of evolution = admit your path is historically contingent.", "no_permanent_optimum": "No permanently optimal strategy exists because market context constantly changes. System maintenance = daily task, not one-time design."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_022">
  <data key="d16">Austrian_Knowledge_Trading</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "奥地利经济学_Hayek_Mises", "knowledge_problem": "You never have complete information. But price itself is a knowledge aggregation mechanism. Respect price as summary of all分散knowledge.", "entrepreneurial_alertness": "Kirzner: profit comes from seeing what others miss. Alertness ≠ more indicators. Train perception to notice differences in familiar patterns.", "subjective_value": "No intrinsic value. Value = each participant's subjective evaluation. Before asking 'what is this worth', ask 'who is pricing it'.", "time_preference": "Your time preference (willingness to wait) determines your suitable strategy. Short-term high time preference → day trading. Long-term low time preference → investing. Strategy must match time preference.", "spontaneous_order": "Market was not designed by anyone. It emerged from millions of non-intentional actions. Your system also emerges from practice, not pure theory. Respect what你cannot know.", "price_signal_dependence": "Without price feedback you cannot evaluate decisions. Distorted prices (manipulation/suspended/illiquid) = corrupted decision feedback."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_023">
  <data key="d16">Margin_of_Safety_System_Design</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "安全边际_Klarman", "expanded_margin": "Safety margin is not a valuation metric (PB&lt;1). It's humility toward uncertainty. The error tolerance your system can absorb.", "avoid_loss_first": "Rule 1: Don't lose money. Rule 2: Don't forget rule 1. Risk management priority IS the source of excess return.", "unconstrained_advantage": "Individual investors' biggest edge = no quarterly performance pressure, no benchmark, no redemption risk. Can wait 3 months for opportunity.", "price_vs_value": "Price is Mr. Market's emotion. Value is your analysis. Price may diverge long-term not because market is wrong but because its pricing logic differs.", "liquidity_risk": "Most underrated risk factor. Evaluate position not by average daily volume but by 'how many days to exit in crisis'. Discount liquidity into safety margin.", "catalyst_requirement": "Cheap without catalyst = value trap. Every buy must answer: what event triggers value回归? Performance improvement/asset disposal/management change/industry cycle.", "cash_as_option": "Cash is not uninvested money. Cash is an active position with value = option to buy low in future crisis.", "depth_over_breadth": "Deep research on few names beats shallow coverage of many. Conviction during price fluctuation comes from depth not diversification."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_024">
  <data key="d16">Fractal_Market_Risk_Framework</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "市场的错误行为_Mandelbrot", "non_normal_distribution": "Markets follow fractal power-law distribution (α≈1.7), not normal distribution. 6σ events occur every few years, not once in 10^18 years. VaR/Sharpe/standard deviation based on normal distribution are dangerous illusions.", "scale_invariance": "Price patterns are self-similar across time scales. 5min chart ≈ daily chart ≈ monthly chart. Your chosen timeframe is a filter/interpretation choice.", "volatility_clustering": "Volatility comes in clusters. Calm follows calm, storm follows storm. Adjust position size to current volatility regime.", "fat_tail_frequency": "Extreme events (7σ in normal) occur every 30-40 years in real markets. Tail risk is structural, not a 'what if'. Tail events can constitute 50% of total risk.", "correlation_breakdown": "Correlations converge to 1.0 during crises. Diversification fails exactly when needed most. Tail risk requires tail hedging not diversification.", "hurst_exponent": "H&gt;0.5 = trending regime, H&lt;0.5 = mean-reverting regime. Identifying current regime (trending vs oscillating) is more important than any specific indicator.", "pattern_skepticism": "Most chart patterns (head-shoulders, double-bottom) can be generated by fractal random processes. Require 100+ sample statistical validation before trusting any pattern."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_025">
  <data key="d16">Predictably_Irrational_Trading_Traps</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "可预测的非理性_Ariely", "decoy_effect": "Others' returns/positions are your decoy. They distort your relative judgment. Block comparison: you need only your own strategy and discipline.", "self_anchoring": "First profitable method anchors all future behavior. Break self-anchoring = evolve. Look only at future expected value, not past patterns.", "free_trap": "Zero-commission → overtrading. Free information → over-reliance. 'Free' is the most expensive in trading as it bypasses理性calculation.", "hot_cold_empathy_gap": "Your calm-state plans (I will definitely stop loss) are invalid in emotional states. Only mechanical rules survive temperature change.", "endowment_effect": "Ownership doubles perceived value. Test: 'If I didn't own this, would I buy it at current price?' If no → sell immediately.", "door_closing_discipline": "Closing positions/deleting watchlists/abandoning strategies is more important than opening new ones. Each open position dilutes attention.", "expectation_filter": "Your expectations filter what you see from data. Before reading data, write the counter-hypothesis first.", "cash_abstraction": "Digital money feels less real than cash. Treat every yuan as cash regardless of source (profit/margin/floating gain).", "external_constraint": "Hard stop order &gt; written plan &gt; self-discipline. Willpower is the most depleted resource by end of trading day."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_026">
  <data key="d16">Classical_Economics_Trading_Principles</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">economics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "Smith_Keynes_边际革命", "invisible_hand_trust": "Good system needs minimal daily intervention. If you're constantly micro-managing, system design is wrong. Trust the rules to produce good long-term results.", "division_of_labor": "Master one pattern (breakout/value/arbitrage) → skill deepens → intuition forms. Specialization is efficiency not limitation.", "marginal_decision": "Only marginal matters: what is the expected value of the NEXT unit? Sunk costs/average costs/past profits are irrelevant.", "Keynes_beauty_contest": "Don't pick what YOU think is beautiful. Pick what you think the judges will think is beautiful. And further: what judges think judges will think. Third-layer reasoning.", "sunk_cost_rule": "你的买入价_已亏金额_历史盈利 = all irrelevant to current decision. Only forward-looking expected value matters."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_027">
  <data key="d16">Cai_Gen_Tan_Trading_Simplicity</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "菜根谭_小窗幽记_围炉夜话", "true_flavor_is_bland": "醲肥辛甘非真味真味只是淡 = complex strategies are not the true way. The best method is simple and plain.", "moderation_in_all": "路径窄处留一步_滋味浓时减三分 = when market is crowded leave room. Let others eat the last bite.", "post_profit_warning": "居盈满者切忌再加一滴 = account full? Don't add a single drop more. Profit → reduce not increase.", "emotional_mastery": "气收自觉怒平_神敛自觉言简 = breathing controls anger, focus controls speech. 冷眼冷耳冷情冷心 = four colds for objective trading.", "error_acceptance": "昨日之非不可留_今日之是不可执 = yesterday's loss don't dwell, today's win don't cling. 知过能改便是圣人之徒 = knowing and correcting error is mastery.", "patience_primacy": "十分不耐烦乃为人大病 = impatience is the great disease. 江山风月闲者为主 = the one who waits is the market's master."}</data>
  <data key="d5">192</data>
</node>
<node id="entity_053_028">
  <data key="d16">Xun_Yue_Three_Mirrors_Self_Knowledge</data>
  <data key="d0">trading_concept</data>
  <data key="d24">chinese_classics_trading</data>
  <data key="d17">{"source": "申鉴_荀悦_杂言", "three_mirrors": {"鉴乎前_history_mirror": "past market data is the best textbook. Learn from historical patterns.", "鉴乎人_others_mirror": "learn from successful traders and be warned by failed ones.", "鉴乎镜_self_record_mirror": "your own trading record is the most honest mirror."}, "decision_hierarchy": "知人_知言_知义 = understand participants → understand market language → understand principle. Reverse: first understand principle, then read market, then know participants.", "contrarian_wisdom": "善钧从众 = true consensus is following what is right, not following the crowd. If crowd does wrong it's not consensus.", "reference_then_decide": "公断优于独断 = decide after wide reference (多因子交叉验证) not before. 参而断谓之公断_不参而断谓之独断.", "bending_to_stretch": "尺蠖之屈以求伸也 = a loss/stop is bending to prepare for next stretch. 屈而不伸失其所以屈 = stop but never re-enter = lost the meaning of stopping."}</data>
  <data key="d5">35</data>
</node>
