<node id="concept_walkthrough_counterfactual_audit">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">走查+反事实复盘 — 交易前情景预演+交易后归因检验</data>
  <data key="d2">reading_notes</data>
  <data key="d3">["stock_data/reading_notes/2026-05-27_卡斯蒂复杂化_不可预测与突现_交易穿透.md"]</data>
  <data key="d4">Casti's walkthrough method: before each trade/trading day, mentally simulate 3 scenarios (bull/bear/shock) and check if your system holds up. After each trade, counterfactual analysis: was profit from skill or luck? Was loss from strategy flaw or market conditions? Distinguishes signal from noise in performance attribution.</data>
  <data key="d5">176</data>
</node>
<node id="concept_self_organized_criticality_risk">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">自组织临界性与幂律尾部保护 — 沙堆模型监控市场风险</data>
  <data key="d2">reading_notes</data>
  <data key="d3">["stock_data/reading_notes/2026-05-27_卡斯蒂复杂化_不可预测与突现_交易穿透.md", "stock_data/reading_notes/2026-05-27_尼科利斯普里戈金探索复杂性_耗散结构_交易穿透.md"]</data>
  <data key="d4">Bak's self-organized criticality (sandpile model): market crashes are not external accidents but the system's normal function for releasing accumulated stress. Monitor crowding/leverage/concentration as 'criticality indicators' — when near critical, reduce exposure (lower the sandpile). Power-law tails demand protection against the one big crash.</data>
  <data key="d5">297</data>
</node>
<node id="concept_jammer_premise_analysis">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">Jammer 前提分析 — 识别策略的不可见假设</data>
  <data key="d2">reading_notes</data>
  <data key="d3">["stock_data/reading_notes/2026-05-26_贾默量子力学概念发展_交易穿透.md"]</data>
  <data key="d4">Jammer's method: trace each concept back to its hidden premises. For trading: list 5 core premises your strategy depends on ('history repeats', 'TA works', 'market has structure'). Ask: if this premise fails, does my strategy collapse? Premise analysis is more fundamental than stop-loss — it controls the strategy's survival conditions.</data>
  <data key="d5">176</data>
</node>
